---
// Terms for people embedding the calculators on their own sites.
//
// This exists because the liability changes shape once a calculator is on
// fifty other websites: a stale rate is then wrong in fifty places, under
// fifty different brands, and none of those firms can fix it themselves.
//
// Kept deliberately short and readable. A wall of legal text on a free tool
// undermines the trust that makes people embed it in the first place.

import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LAST_VERIFIED } from '../components/tools/taxData.js';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Embed terms | gazza.ltd"
  description="The terms for embedding gazza.ltd calculators on your own website."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={[
      { name: 'Embed a calculator', href: '/embed' },
      { name: 'Terms' },
    ]} />

    <h1>Embed terms</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      Short version: use them freely, keep the credit link, and don't present
      the results as professional advice.
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What you may do</h2>
      <p>
        Embed any calculator listed on <a href="/embed">the embed page</a> on any
        website, including a commercial one, at no cost and without asking
        permission. You may embed as many as you like, on as many pages as you
        like. You may set the width, height and border to suit your layout.
      </p>

      <h2>What we ask</h2>
      <p>
        Keep the credit link that comes with the snippet, visible and
        followable, on the same page as the calculator. That link is the only
        thing we get in return, and it's what makes the calculators free.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please don't imply that gazza.ltd endorses you, your firm or your
        services, and don't present the calculator as your own product.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy, and what you're responsible for</h2>
      <p>
        We take the figures seriously. Tax bands, thresholds and reliefs come
        from HMRC, Revenue Scotland and the Welsh Revenue Authority, each
        calculator's maths is tested against worked examples published by those
        bodies, and the verification date — currently {LAST_VERIFIED} — is shown
        inside the calculator so your visitors can judge it for themselves.
      </p>
      <p>
        That said, the calculators are provided as-is, without warranty. They
        are general information, not financial, legal, tax or professional
        advice. If you are regulated — a mortgage broker, a solicitor, an
        accountant — you remain responsible for what appears on your own website
        and for any advice you give based on it. Check anything that matters
        against the official source.
      </p>
      <p>
        We aren't liable for losses arising from use of the calculators, whether
        on this site or embedded on yours.
      </p>

      <h2>Updates and availability</h2>
      <p>
        The calculators are served from gazza.ltd, so we can and do update them
        — when rates change, your embed changes with them, usually within
        minutes and with nothing required from you. The flip side is that if
        this site is down, the calculator on your page won't load. We don't
        offer an uptime guarantee.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may change or retire a calculator. If we ever retire one that's in
        active use we'll leave the URL working and tell anyone who has been in
        touch, but we can't promise a URL will exist forever.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The embedded calculators run entirely in the visitor's browser. Nothing
        anyone types is transmitted to us or stored. We set no cookies in the
        embed and there are no adverts or tracking scripts inside it, so
        embedding a calculator shouldn't require any change to your cookie
        banner or privacy policy. Our own site's
        <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> covers gazza.ltd itself.
      </p>

      <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, problems, or a calculator you'd like that we don't have:
        <a href="mailto:hello@gazza.ltd">hello@gazza.ltd</a>. If you tell us
        where you've embedded one, we'll let you know before anything changes
        that would affect you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
